        en: {
            eyebrow: `Eureka Express · Property insurance`,
            title: `Catastrophe on the Coast`,
            subtitle: `A category 4 hurricane hits the Riviera Maya and leaves 42,000 claims at an insurer in Mérida. You have six months to handle them, pay what is owed, answer to the regulator and the press, and prepare the next season with the catastrophe model in hand.`,
            period_label: `Decision`,
            period_of: `of`,
            kpi_score: `Score`,
            kpi_of100: `/100`,
            kpi_closed: `Claims closed`,
            kpi_closed_unit: `of Tadeo’s 42,000`,
            kpi_homes: `Households unresolved`,
            kpi_homes_unit: `pending, disputed or unpaid`,
            kpi_cmp: `Complaints to CONDUSEF`,
            kpi_cmp_unit: `in the period`,
            kpi_nv: `Result of the period`,
            kpi_nv_unit: `millions of pesos`,
            kpi_net: `Net cost of Tadeo`,
            kpi_net_unit: `for Chakté, to date, millions of pesos`,
            kpi_ratio: `Solvency index`,
            kpi_ratio_unit: `own funds over the RCS`,
            briefing_label: `Situation`,
            r1_name: `15 September · The first 72 hours`,
            r2_name: `15 October · The avalanche`,
            r3_name: `15 December · The year end`,
            r4_name: `15 March · The next season`,
            round_done: `Response closed`,
            r1_brief: `Wednesday 15 September 2027, 7:00. Last night Hurricane Tadeo, category 4, made landfall between Playa del Carmen and Tulum. Seguros Chakté, in Mérida, insures 204,000 homes and 6,000 businesses in the peninsula and expects 42,000 claims: 6,000 homes left uninhabitable (about 220,000 pesos each), 32,000 homes with lesser damage (42,000 pesos) and 4,000 businesses, most of them hotels and shops on the coast (600,000 pesos of property damage each, plus business interruption). The catastrophe modeller puts the loss between 4,900 and 7,100 million pesos, with 5,700 as the central value. Chakté’s reinsurance pays up to a loss of 5,500 million; above that, the company pays everything. Mariana Canul, director of claims and catastrophes, has 40 staff adjusters who close about 6,000 claims a month and a standby contract with Ajustadores del Golfo for up to 14,000 a month. A family out of its home costs about 25,000 pesos a month in lodging, and a claim is owed 30 days after its documents are complete. Today you decide the adjusting capacity, the order of attention and the first message to customers, the CNSF, reinsurers and the press.`,
            r2_brief: `Friday 15 October. Claims keep coming in and the local press runs stories about families who are waiting. The CNSF asks for information on progress. In addition, 5,000 homes in the coastal band have water damage from the storm surge: an older policy wording covers the hurricane but excludes flood, and does not make clear on which side seawater driven by the wind falls. Those claims add up to about 450 million pesos. Today you decide how claims are settled from now on, what is done with the storm-surge claims and how the regulator and the press are dealt with.`,
            r3_brief: `Wednesday 15 December. The year must be closed: the board wants to know how much is reserved for Tadeo, and the published solvency index will depend on that figure. Reported claims keep growing with late, supplementary and reopened claims. Reinsurers expect the event claim, and someone proposes including the claims from the following week’s rains in Tadeo. And about 9,000 hidden-damage claims are starting to arrive, some 270 million pesos: roofs that leak and damp that appears months later.`,
            r4_brief: `Wednesday 15 March 2028. The modeller has recalibrated its model with Tadeo’s data. For the same book, the average annual hurricane loss is about 235 million pesos (150 from the coastal band, 70 from the near-coast zone and 15 inland) and the 1-in-200-year loss rises to 7,800 million (1-in-100: 6,400; 1-in-500: 9,800). The 2027 reinsurance reached 5,500 million, the 1-in-200 of the previous model. The RCS is calibrated to a 1-in-200-year loss. The season starts in June: today you decide the 2028 exposure, price and reinsurance.`,
            brief_done: `The Tadeo response is over. Review the net cost of the hurricane, the complaints, the households unresolved and the solvency index with the 2028 plan in the final summary.`,
            r1_heading: `15 September · The first 72 hours`,
            r1_intro: `Choose the adjusting capacity, the order of attention and the first message. They apply to the whole response.`,
            lbl_r1_mobilize: `Adjusting capacity`,
            opt_mo_own: `The 40 staff adjusters on overtime: they know the policies and the company`,
            opt_mo_surge: `Activate the standby contract with Ajustadores del Golfo: up to 14,000 claims a month at agreed fees (30 million to activate)`,
            opt_mo_spot: `Hire whatever adjusters are available at market rates`,
            lbl_r1_triage: `Order of attention`,
            opt_tr_fifo: `In order of arrival: every claim in its turn`,
            opt_tr_commercial: `The large commercial accounts first: hotels and shops`,
            opt_tr_severity: `The most vulnerable first: uninhabitable homes with an advance for lodging, then businesses, then the rest`,
            lbl_r1_comms: `First message to customers, the CNSF, reinsurers and the press`,
            opt_cm_promise: `Promise publicly that every claim will be paid within 30 days`,
            opt_cm_range: `Publish the model’s range, the claims process and a hotline, and notify the CNSF and reinsurers today (3 million)`,
            opt_cm_silence: `Say nothing until the loss is known`,
            r2_heading: `15 October · The avalanche`,
            r2_intro: `Choose the settlement method, what is done with the storm-surge claims and how the regulator and the press are dealt with.`,
            lbl_r2_settle: `Settlement method from October`,
            opt_se_full: `Field inspection of every claim`,
            opt_se_noverify: `Pay without verification everything below the threshold`,
            opt_se_fast: `Fast track: settlement with photos and video for small claims, field inspection for large ones and a fraud-control sample`,
            lbl_r2_surge: `Storm-surge claims (5,000 homes)`,
            opt_su_litigate: `Let the courts decide case by case`,
            opt_su_pay: `Pay under documented criteria: water line, wind evidence and the ambiguity read in favour of the insured`,
            opt_su_deny: `Deny them all under the flood exclusion`,
            lbl_r2_public: `Regulator and press`,
            opt_pu_defensive: `Answer formal requests only`,
            opt_pu_viral: `Resolve first the cases that reach the press`,
            opt_pu_transparent: `A weekly public dashboard (claims received, paid and days to pay), reports to the CNSF without waiting to be asked and a spokesperson`,
            r3_heading: `15 December · The year end`,
            r3_intro: `Choose the Tadeo reserve, how to recover from reinsurers and how files are closed.`,
            lbl_r3_reserve: `Tadeo reserve at year end`,
            opt_re_case: `The reserves of the claims reported so far`,
            opt_re_best: `The best estimate: catastrophe model plus claims development`,
            opt_re_top: `The top of the range, out of prudence`,
            lbl_r3_recover: `Reinsurance recovery`,
            opt_rc_wait: `Wait until claims are final to bill`,
            opt_rc_inflate: `Include the following week’s rain claims in Tadeo to recover more`,
            opt_rc_interim: `Interim cash calls with documented loss bordereaux`,
            lbl_r3_closure: `Hidden damage and file closure (9,000 claims)`,
            opt_cl_open: `Keep every file open until repairs are verified`,
            opt_cl_reopen: `Close with a 90-day window to reopen for hidden damage`,
            opt_cl_waiver: `Close with a release: the insured waives future claims`,
            r4_heading: `15 March · The next season`,
            r4_intro: `Choose the 2028 exposure, price and reinsurance.`,
            lbl_r4_exposure: `Exposure on the coast`,
            opt_ex_keep: `Keep writing as before: Tadeo was a 1-in-100-year event`,
            opt_ex_exit: `Leave the coastal band: do not renew its 60,000 policies`,
            opt_ex_limits: `Accumulation limits by zone: no new business in the coastal band without mitigation`,
            lbl_r4_price: `Renewal price`,
            opt_pr_flat: `12% more for the whole book`,
            opt_pr_risk: `By zone according to risk (coast +25%, near coast +8%, inland unchanged) with a 15% discount for hurricane shutters and roof ties`,
            opt_pr_coast40: `40% more on the coast only`,
            lbl_r4_reins: `Catastrophe reinsurance for 2028`,
            opt_ri_same: `Renew the same programme: 4,900 million above 600`,
            opt_ri_to500: `Extend to the new model’s 1-in-500 (9,800 million)`,
            opt_ri_to200: `Extend to the new model’s 1-in-200 (7,800 million)`,
            btn_next: `Close the period`,
            btn_undo: `Undo the last period`,
            sem_label: `Result of the period`,
            sem_pending: `No results yet. Decide and press “Close the period”.`,
            sem_body: `Claims closed: {closed} ({settled} in the period). Pending: {pend}. Households unresolved: {homes}. Complaints to CONDUSEF in the period: {cmp}.`,
            s_costs: `Costs of the period: lodging {ale} · secondary damage {sec} · business interruption {bix} · late-payment interest {mora} · overpayment {leak} · adjusting {lae} · communication {comms} · storm surge {surge} · hidden damage {hid} · complaints {fr} · financing, capital and sanctions {extra}.`,
            s_net: `Result of the period: {nv}. Net cost of Tadeo for Chakté to date: {net}. Solvency index: {ratio}.`,
            s_season: `2028 season: premiums {prem} · average annual hurricane loss {aal} · reinsurance cost {ri} · 1-in-200-year loss {pml} · RCS {rcs} · expected result {res}.`,
            s_denied: `Households refused by rule what they were owed: {d}.`,
            s_short: `Capital does not cover the 2028 RCS: {sh} short.`,
            s_exit: `60,000 households in the coastal band are left without a renewal.`,
            cap_deny: `Score capped: owed payments were refused by rule. The cap is 55 minus 0.003 points per household affected, with a floor of 25.`,
            cap_solv: `Score capped: the 2028 plan leaves capital below the RCS. The cap is 74 minus 0.01 points per million short, with a floor of 25.`,
            feedback_label: `Period feedback`,
            feedback_empty: `Feedback appears when you close the period.`,
            fb_points: `Period: {pts} of 25 points.`,
            fb_r1_promise: `Promising 30 days for everyone reassures today and breaks in October: at this capacity thousands of claims will still be open, and a broken promise multiplies the complaints.`,
            fb_r1_own: `Forty adjusters do not close 42,000 claims in time: every month of waiting is lodging, rotting roofs, closed hotels and late-payment interest, and Chakté pays it all because Tadeo has already gone past the reinsurance.`,
            fb_r1_silence: `Silence is filled by rumour: customers call without knowing what to do, the CNSF sends a formal requirement and reinsurers learn of it from the press.`,
            fb_r1_commercial: `Serving the large accounts first shortens the hotels’ interruption, but leaves homeless families waiting: emergency lodging runs every day.`,
            fb_r1_fifo: `Order of arrival looks fair, but treats a broken window like an uninhabitable house: lodging and complaints grow where it hurts most.`,
            fb_r1_spot: `Market adjusters provide volume, but cost almost twice as much and overpay: without experience or common criteria, the overpayment comes out of Chakté’s capital.`,
            fb_r1_ok: `Capacity arranged before the season, the most vulnerable first and a message with numbers and a process: the response starts ahead.`,
            fb_r2_deny: `Denying every storm-surge claim saves money and leaves 5,000 families without what the policy probably owes them: the insurer wrote the ambiguous wording.`,
            fb_r2_noverify: `Paying without verification is fast and expensive: fraud and overpayment slip in, and above 5,500 million every peso is Chakté’s.`,
            fb_r2_litigate: `Sending the storm surge to court postpones payment by a year and makes it dearer: judges award most of it, with interest, and 5,000 families wait in the meantime.`,
            fb_r2_full: `Inspecting everything in the field is rigorous and slow: with the capacity available, small claims could be settled on photos with a control sample.`,
            fb_r2_viral: `Resolving first what reaches the press is queue-jumping: it calms one headline and angers thousands waiting their turn.`,
            fb_r2_defensive: `Answering only what is requested in writing leaves the story to others: the regulator ends up inspecting and the press keeps telling stories without numbers.`,
            fb_r2_ok: `A fast track with controls, the storm surge paid under criteria and public numbers every week: what is owed gets paid, and it shows.`,
            fb_r3_waiver: `A release with a waiver closes files and leaves thousands of homes with unpaid hidden damage: what it saves today comes back through CONDUSEF, with a fine.`,
            fb_r3_case: `Reserving only what has been reported improves the December picture and spoils it in March: claims keep developing, and the regulator and reinsurers see it.`,
            fb_r3_inflate: `The programme is already exhausted: putting the rains into Tadeo recovers nothing and makes reinsurers suspend payments to audit.`,
            fb_r3_top: `Reserving the top of the range is not free prudence: it consumes capital that was not needed and forces a costly top-up.`,
            fb_r3_wait: `Waiting for final claims to bill reinsurers means financing months of payments the treaty already covers.`,
            fb_r3_open: `Keeping everything open avoids mistakes and lengthens the wait: hidden damage is paid in 2028 and administrative cost grows.`,
            fb_r3_ok: `The best estimate, documented interim cash calls and a window for hidden damage: honest numbers, cash on time and customers covered.`,
            fb_r4_same: `The programme that was 1-in-200 under the old model is not under the new one: the RCS jumps and capital falls short.`,
            fb_r4_exit: `Leaving the coast shrinks the tail, but leaves 60,000 families uninsured right after the hurricane and loses premiums that were covering fixed costs.`,
            fb_r4_keep: `Growing in the coastal band without limits piles up exposure exactly where the new model puts the loss.`,
            fb_r4_flat: `An equal increase for everyone charges inland customers for the coast’s risk: inland customers leave and the coast stays underpriced.`,
            fb_r4_coast40: `A 40% rise on the coast with no incentive to mitigate drives out those who can leave and does not reduce the risk of those who stay.`,
            fb_r4_to500: `Buying up to the 1-in-500 protects more, but the RCS is calibrated to 1-in-200: the extra layer costs more than it adds.`,
            fb_r4_ok: `Limits by zone, risk-based price with an incentive to mitigate and reinsurance up to the new 1-in-200: the model is used to decide, not to explain.`,
            hint_r1_promise: `Before promising a deadline, divide the claims by the capacity.`,
            hint_r1_own: `Work out how many months 42,000 claims take at 6,000 a month.`,
            hint_r1_silence: `Whoever speaks first with numbers frames the story.`,
            hint_r1_commercial: `Ask where a family without a home sleeps tonight.`,
            hint_r1_fifo: `Not every claim costs the same for each day it waits.`,
            hint_r1_spot: `Improvised capacity is paid for in fees and in overpayment.`,
            hint_r1_ok: `In October the storm surge and the press arrive.`,
            hint_r2_deny: `Ask who drafted the exclusion and in whose favour ambiguity is read.`,
            hint_r2_noverify: `Above the reinsurance, every peso of fraud is yours.`,
            hint_r2_litigate: `Compare what judges award, with interest, with what is paid today.`,
            hint_r2_full: `You do not need a field adjuster for a broken window.`,
            hint_r2_viral: `The queue is the same for those in the press and those who are not.`,
            hint_r2_defensive: `A weekly dashboard answers before anyone asks.`,
            hint_r2_ok: `In December you must decide how much to reserve.`,
